               <P>Our build process is pretty seamless all the way through to an Integration environment which sits right between Development (laptop/workstation) and Certification (keep your muddy paws off land).&nbsp; With this automation and continuous integration in general, comes a large amount of excess in the form of intermediate versions.&nbsp; During a recent upgrade to Window 2003 (don’t ask why it took so long) we found that the little utility that keeps this Integration environment clean started getting fussy.&nbsp; Well it turns out that you have to install the WMI Windows Installer Provider explicitly.&nbsp; Here’s how to find it:<o:p></o:p></P>
